<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

<details>
<summary>Why does the tuner keep the microphone on?</summary>
<p>Real-time pitch display requires continuous listening. The audio is
<strong>analyzed on-device and discarded immediately</strong> — never recorded, stored, or uploaded.
See our <a href="./privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
</details>

<details>
<summary>Where are my recordings stored? Are they uploaded?</summary>
<p>Everything stays on your device and is <strong>never uploaded</strong>. There are no accounts and no
servers. Note that deleting the app also deletes all of its data — please export a backup first if you
have recordings you want to keep.</p>
</details>

<details>
<summary>Can I move my data to a new device?</summary>
<p>Yes. Use the in-app Backup/Export feature on the old device, then Restore/Import on the new one.</p>
</details>

<details>
<summary>Does the metronome keep playing when the screen is locked?</summary>
<p>Yes, background playback is supported. If audio stops, check that Low Power Mode is off and that no
other app has taken over audio.</p>
</details>

<details>
<summary>Recording is silent or too quiet</summary>
<p>Check that microphone access is enabled in iOS Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Microphone; that the
device is not muted; that you try the built-in microphone if using Bluetooth headphones; and that the
input gain in the recording screen is not set too low.</p>
</details>

<h2>Privacy</h2>
<p>Beat Partner <strong>collects no personal data</strong> — no accounts, no tracking, no ads.
See the full <a href="./privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

